# Optional settings. Copy to .env if you like; claudecord does not read .env itself, so export these in your shell or put them in
# the systemd unit. NONE of these are secrets: the Discord token, the OAuth secret and bucket keys are never environment
# variables. They are sealed in the hosted service's data folder, or live in files there (mode 0600) written by
# `claudecord-hub storage ...`.

# How much is logged: error, warn, info (default) or debug.
# CLAUDECORD_LOG=info

# Where a machine keeps its login, daemon socket and per-agent logs (default: ~/.claudecord).
# CLAUDECORD_HOME=

# Machine placement: how many agents this machine should run at once, and labels such as gpu.
# CLAUDECORD_MAX_AGENTS=8
# CLAUDECORD_LABELS=gpu,fast

# How agents run: tmux (default where installed) or pty (the built-in terminal, used on native Windows).
# CLAUDECORD_TERMINAL=tmux
# The name of the private tmux server claudecord uses, so it never touches your own tmux.
# CLAUDECORD_TMUX_SOCKET=claudecord

# npm package only: run this program instead of the platform package's (for development).
# CLAUDECORD_BINARY=
